  "reading": "CORRECTED. These probes are fitted once on train_observed_successor and applied to observed, generated and reset latents alike (gate.py:1784), while the action-only baseline is fitted natively, so generated-condition comparisons against it are transfer-handicapped. In domain, [z,h] beats action-only by about +0.09 in both arms and the strided arm is marginally better (+0.099 vs +0.092). h alone beats it by +0.04 to +0.05 with no transfer penalty, its observed and generated scores being identical. The deficit is specific to generated z, which drags the joint readout below the floor; whether that is missing information or a decoder fitted in the wrong subspace is not settled here. The earlier reading -- that no arm beats action-only and that h's advantage is merely action information -- was drawn from the generated column alone and is withdrawn.",
